// Shared RIVTA building block: TimeStampType.
//
// This file is deliberately NOT a real conversion. TimeStampType is a plain, pattern-
// constrained xs:string in the RIVTA schema (YYYYMMDDhhmmss, Europe/Stockholm local time,
// see clinicalprocess_healthcond_description_2.1.xsd) - generateDS therefore hands it to FML
// as an ordinary Python str, with no date semantics attached at all. GENERAL-001 requires a
// DST-aware Europe/Stockholm -> explicit-UTC-offset (or true-UTC "Z" instant) conversion, and
// there is no FHIRPath/FML function that can compute a historical DST offset for an arbitrary
// date (FHIRPath has no timezone-database access). This is the exact same conclusion the
// HAPI/FML track reached (fml-evaluation.md, GENERAL-001: "FML-reglerna kopierar bara redan-
// konverterade strängar rakt av") and it holds for MaLaC-HD too: the conversion MUST happen
// before the value reaches any .map file.
//
// In this track that pre-conversion is preprocess.py (the Python equivalent of
// RivDateParser.parse()/parseInstant()), run once per fixture against a copy of the raw
// RIVTA XML before MaLaC-HD ever sees it. Every other .map file in this proof of concept
// (get-diagnosis-to-condition.map, get-diagnosis-to-provenance.map, and
// lib-legal-authenticator-type.map's assertedDate group) assumes its TimeStampType-typed
// source fields are ALREADY ISO-8601 strings with an explicit offset (or "Z") by the time
// FML sees them, and simply copies the string across - which is itself the one concrete
// thing worth demonstrating here: a plain generateDS string value CAN be assigned directly
// to a FHIR dateTime/instant target field without any create()/cast ceremony, once the text
// is already valid ISO-8601 (verified against both RivDateParser.parse()'s dateTime shape and
// RivDateParser.parseInstant()'s instant shape as part of this proof of concept, see
// malac-hd-evaluation.md, "RivDateParser-motsvarigheten").
map "http://ehds-brygga.inera.se/fhir/StructureMap/LibTimeStampType" = "LibTimeStampType"

uses "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/string" alias PreConvertedTimestamp as source
uses "http://hl7.org/fhir/StructureDefinition/Extension" alias Extension as target

group TimeStampToExtensionValue(source src : PreConvertedTimestamp, target tgt : Extension) {
  src -> tgt.value = src "timestamp-value";
}
